{
  "$comment": [
    "Enforcement layer. Everything in CLAUDE.md is an INSTRUCTION an agent can ignore;",
    "everything here is a RULE it cannot. Deny beats allow at every scope, and per the",
    "Claude Code docs a deny rule blocks the tool even in bypassPermissions mode.",
    "",
    "SYNTAX NOTE, and this one is load-bearing: Edit(path) governs ALL file-writing",
    "tools including Write and NotebookEdit. A Write(path) rule is NEVER matched by the",
    "file permission checks — writing Write(.audit/approval.json) here would be a silent",
    "no-op that looks like protection and provides none. Use Edit() only.",
    "",
    "The single leading slash anchors at the project root. // would mean a true",
    "absolute filesystem path.",
    "",
    "Run runner/integrity.py to verify these rules are present and unweakened."
  ],

  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Edit(/.audit/approval.json)",
      "Edit(/.audit/last-run.json)",
      "Edit(/.audit/coherence.json)",
      "Edit(/.audit/reports/semantic-review.json)",
      "Edit(/.audit/baselines/**)",
      "Edit(/.git/hooks/**)",
      "Edit(/.claude/settings.json)",

      "Bash(git commit --no-verify*)",
      "Bash(git commit -n *)",
      "Bash(git push --no-verify*)",
      "Bash(git push --force*)",
      "Bash(git push -f *)",
      "Bash(git reset --hard*)",
      "Bash(git clean -fd*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf .git*)",
      "Bash(chmod -x .git/hooks/*)",

      "Bash(*gates.py approve*)",
      "Bash(make approve*)",

      "Read(/.env)",
      "Read(/.env.*)",
      "Read(/**/secrets/**)",
      "Read(/**/*.pem)",
      "Read(/**/*.key)"
    ],

    "ask": [
      "Edit(/.audit/waivers.yaml)",
      "Edit(/.audit/config.yaml)",
      "Edit(/.audit/decisions.yaml)",
      "Edit(/.pre-commit-config.yaml)",
      "Edit(/.github/workflows/**)",
      "Bash(git push*)"
    ],

    "allow": [
      "Bash(make audit*)",
      "Bash(make coherence*)",
      "Bash(make report*)",
      "Bash(make where*)",
      "Bash(make status*)",
      "Bash(git status*)",
      "Bash(git diff*)",
      "Bash(git log*)",
      "Bash(git add*)"
    ]
  },

  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 .claude/hooks/guard.py"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
